So: $$
M = \text{number of unacquainted pairs with at least one common acquaintance}
$$

Hence, in the Turán graph: $$
M = \text{number of non-edges} = \binom{\lfloor n/2 \rfloor}{2} + \binom{\lceil n/2 \rceil}{2}
$$

Then: $$
M = \binom{a}{2} + \binom{b}{2}
$$

But since $ a + b = n $, and $ b = n - a $, we can write: $$
M = \binom{a}{2} + \binom{n - a}{2}
$$

Let’s simplify this: $$
\binom{a}{2} + \binom{n - a}{2}
= \frac{a(a - 1)}{2} + \frac{(n - a)(n - a - 1)}{2}
$$

Let’s define $ a = \lfloor n/2 \rfloor $, $ b = \lceil n/2 \rceil $, and write: $$
M = \binom{a}{2} + \binom{b}{2}
$$

### ✅ Final Answer: $$
\boxed{\binom{\left\lfloor \frac{n}{2} \right\rfloor}{2} + \binom{\left\lceil \frac{n}{2} \right\rceil}{2}}
$$
